    {
      "skill_id": "de-a1-014",
      "title": "Personal pronouns: nominative and selected accusative",
      "explanation": "Personal pronouns replace nouns. Nominative (subject): ich, du, er, sie, es, wir, ihr, sie, Sie. Accusative (direct object) for frequent forms: mich, dich, ihn, sie, es, uns, euch, sie, Sie. Only some forms change: er becomes ihn, ich becomes mich, du becomes dich, wir becomes uns, ihr becomes euch; sie, es and Sie stay the same. Compare Ich kenne dich (I know you) with Du kennst mich (you know me).",
      "examples": [
        {
          "de": "Ich kenne dich.",
          "en": "I know you."
        },
        {
          "de": "Er sieht mich.",
          "en": "He sees me."
        },
        {
          "de": "Wir kennen ihn.",
          "en": "We know him."
        }
      ],
