      "skill_id": "de-a1-016",
      "title": "Modal verbs with an infinitive at the end",
      "explanation": "Modal verbs such as können (can), müssen (must), wollen (want to) and dürfen (may) are irregular in the singular: ich kann, du kannst, er kann; ich muss, du musst, er muss; ich will, du willst, er will; ich darf, du darfst, er darf. The wir and sie forms are the infinitive (wir können). The modal is the finite verb in second position and the main verb stays in its infinitive form at the very end of the clause: Ich kann heute arbeiten.",
      "examples": [
        {
          "de": "Ich kann Deutsch sprechen.",
          "en": "I can speak German."
        },
        {
          "de": "Anna muss heute arbeiten.",
          "en": "Anna has to work today."
        },
        {
          "de": "Wir wollen Fußball spielen.",
          "en": "We want to play football."
        }
      ],
